1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,242
Patchwork turns good intentions into a practical neighbourhood plan. I built this

2
00:00:04,242 --> 00:00:08,485
individual project to explore an open web where agents help people organize

3
00:00:08,485 --> 00:00:11,667
and create, while the person keeps the final decision.

4
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:17,140
Finding a way to help means comparing opportunities, understanding the time involved,

5
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:21,614
and deciding what to do next. Patchwork brings those steps into one

6
00:00:21,614 --> 00:00:26,088
visual workspace. The starter catalogue uses demonstration projects, not a verified live

7
00:00:26,088 --> 00:00:26,833
neighbourhood feed.

8
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:31,822
The website exposes four structured Web M C P tools to an

9
00:00:31,822 --> 00:00:35,812
external browser agent. There is no embedded chatbot. These tools were discovered

10
00:00:35,812 --> 00:00:39,801
and called on the public Cloudflare site. This video is an edited

11
00:00:39,801 --> 00:00:43,125
walkthrough of the captured results, not a continuous screen recording.

12
00:00:44,125 --> 00:00:48,255
For a gardening and food request, the agent calls search neighborhood projects

13
00:00:48,255 --> 00:00:52,386
with a three hour per-project limit. The website returns the orchard and

14
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:56,516
pantry records and updates the visible search. The agent works with project

15
00:00:56,516 --> 00:00:59,958
identifiers and structured data, rather than guessing where to click.

16
00:01:00,958 --> 00:01:05,075
Next, build action plan selects the orchard and pantry: two projects, three

17
00:01:05,075 --> 00:01:09,191
hours total. The tool updates the same React state used by the

18
00:01:09,191 --> 00:01:13,307
page. The person can inspect or remove projects manually. The agent chooses

19
00:01:13,307 --> 00:01:15,708
the combination; the tool reports its total.

20
00:01:16,708 --> 00:01:20,615
The agent can also draft a new need: Map accessible shade. The

21
00:01:20,615 --> 00:01:24,522
proposal tool returns human approval required, with published set to false. Patchwork

22
00:01:24,522 --> 00:01:28,429
shows the draft beside Reject and Approve controls. A tool call alone

23
00:01:28,429 --> 00:01:30,708
does not add it to the catalogue.

24
00:01:31,708 --> 00:01:35,947
For this demonstration, browser automation exercises the separate approval button. The draft

25
00:01:35,947 --> 00:01:40,186
then joins the local catalogue and plan. After a reload, it is

26
00:01:40,186 --> 00:01:44,424
still there. Publishing here means saving on this browser and device, not

27
00:01:44,424 --> 00:01:47,250
sharing with other users or a community database.

28
00:01:48,250 --> 00:01:52,587
The pledge tool prepares a contribution draft and returns confirmation required. It

29
00:01:52,587 --> 00:01:56,924
does not submit anything or contact an organizer. This prototype deliberately stops

30
00:01:56,924 --> 00:02:01,262
at drafting. That limitation is explicit, so neither the agent nor the

31
00:02:01,262 --> 00:02:03,792
demonstration implies a real-world commitment was made.

32
00:02:04,792 --> 00:02:09,667
Implementation uses React and TypeScript, built with Vinext for Cloudflare Pages. A

33
00:02:09,667 --> 00:02:14,542
reusable hook registers tool names, descriptions, input schemas, and handlers, with a

34
00:02:14,542 --> 00:02:19,417
navigator compatibility fallback and cleanup. Tool handlers update shared state; validated local

35
00:02:19,417 --> 00:02:21,042
storage restores supported data.

36
00:02:22,042 --> 00:02:27,392
Thirty-nine automated checks passed in the previous validated run, covering state, persistence,

37
00:02:27,392 --> 00:02:32,742
approval, and interface behavior. Those tests use a model-context shim. Native browser

38
00:02:32,742 --> 00:02:38,092
tool calls provide separate compatibility evidence. Codex helped with implementation, debugging, testing,

39
00:02:38,092 --> 00:02:39,875
documentation, and this walkthrough.

40
00:02:40,875 --> 00:02:44,989
Open the live site in a Web M C P capable browser

41
00:02:44,989 --> 00:02:49,102
and try the documented prompts. The source, MIT license, and testing guide

42
00:02:49,102 --> 00:02:53,216
are public. Patchwork shows how agents can reduce coordination work while people

43
00:02:53,216 --> 00:02:55,958
keep the final decision. Small actions. Shared momentum.
